# Title Vs PDF Name Mismatch

Updated: 2026-09-15
Date first noted: 2026-09-15

## Summary

There is an open question about whether the displayed document title and the underlying PDF filename are mismatching in both FSR v1 and FSR v2.

## Current concern

The original note flags this as something to check, but does not yet record:

- how often it happens
- whether the mismatch is in v1 only, v2 only, or both
- whether the source of truth should be the parsed title, the filename, or another metadata field

## Why this matters

If title and filename diverge, the issue could affect debugging, user trust, retrieval result presentation, and any logic that assumes one field can stand in for the other.

## Current status

Needs investigation. No root cause is captured yet.

## Next checks

1. Sample affected docs from FSR v1 and FSR v2.
2. Compare PDF filename, parsed title, stored metadata title, and UI-facing label.
3. Confirm whether the mismatch is introduced during parsing, ingestion, metadata normalization, or display.

